            <h1>Permission Keys Reference</h1>
          
          <p>Permissions are represented as <b>keys</b>, each serving as a unique identifier for a specific permission. One or more keys can be grouped together and assigned to a <b>keychain</b>.<br></p>
<div class="alert alert-info" role="alert"><div class="h4 alert-heading" role="heading">Customizable Permissions</div>
<p>Default permissions can be easily customized by simply creating your own keychains and roles.</div></p>
<div class="alert alert-info" role="alert"><div class="h4 alert-heading" role="heading">Contributing to Permission Keys</div>
<p>To contribute permission keys, see the <a href='/extensibility/authorization'>Authorization Extensibility Documentation</a>. This guide explains Meshery&rsquo;s extensible authorization system.</div></p>
